Lagoon @VERSION@ - network shares as Amiga volumes

Lagoon mounts SMB 2/3 shares (Windows, macOS, Samba, NAS boxes), AFP
volumes (older Macs) and NFS exports (Unix, Linux) as AmigaDOS volumes,
over any TCP/IP stack (Riptide, Roadshow, Miami, AmiTCP, Genesis). It
also shares the Amiga's own folders with Windows, macOS and Linux (SMB),
for guests or for users with a password.

Requirements: a 68020 or better, AmigaOS 3.0 (V39) or newer, a running
TCP/IP stack.

Installation: double-click Install_Lagoon. It copies

    L:lagoon-handler         the file system handler
    C:Lagoon                 MOUNT, UNMOUNT, LIST, MOUNTALL ...,
                             SHARE, USER, SERVE
    SYS:Prefs/LagoonPrefs    the share list editor
    LOCALE:Catalogs/         German, French, Spanish, Italian

and adds "Lagoon MOUNTALL WAIT 30 >NIL:" and "Run >NIL: Lagoon SERVE AUTO
WAIT 30" (the file server, when "Start at boot" is ticked) to
S:User-Startup.

Then open SYS:Prefs/LagoonPrefs, press "Browse network..." (or "Add..."),
choose the server and the share, "Test" it, tick "Mount at startup" and
press "Save". "Mount" mounts it at once.

To share Amiga folders: LagoonPrefs, "Sharing...", "Add...", pick the
folder, tick "Allow guests" or add a user under "Users...", then "Start
server". Other computers open \\AMIGA\<share> (Windows) or
smb://amiga.local/<share> (Mac, Linux). Only on a network you trust: the
transfers are signed but not encrypted.

The manual is in Docs/ (README.md, install.md, prefs.md, server.md).

